cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "IronMule: a local MLX inference runtime that measures before it optimises"
message: "If you use IronMule or its measurements, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: Tobayko
    website: "https://github.com/Tobayko"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tobayko/IronMule"
abstract: >-
  IronMule is a local inference runtime for MLX on Apple silicon. It provides
  explicit execution plans, grouped batch-1 execution at width four, a safe
  sequential fallback, and telemetry that separates service time-to-first-token
  from engine time-to-first-token. Every performance claim is backed by a
  preregistered experiment with raw data, including four optimisations that were
  measured and dropped.
keywords:
  - MLX
  - Apple silicon
  - LLM inference
  - inference runtime
  - KV cache
  - prefix caching
  - batching
  - reproducible research
license: "IronMule License 2.0"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-25"
